[36mCEO (Planner)[0m   "target_users": "Developers, students, sysadmins, QA engineers, and anyone who needs quick temperature conversions on the command line or in scripts. Also useful in automation pipelines where a simple temperature conversion utility is required.",
[36mCEO (Planner)[0m   "features": [
[36mCEO (Planner)[0m    "Interactive mode (default when run with no flags): shows a simple numbered menu with options: 1) Celsius → Fahrenheit, 2) Fahrenheit → Celsius, 3) Batch from stdin/file, 4) Change precision, 5) Exit. Menu repeats until user exits.",
[36mCEO (Planner)[0m    "Interactive conversion flow: after selecting direction, prompt for a temperature value (single value). Accepts plain numbers, optional unit suffixes (e.g., '100', '100C', '32F', '32°F'), handles whitespace, and returns a formatted conversion result including input, converted value, formula used, and units.",
[36mCEO (Planner)[0m    "Non-interactive (scriptable) mode via flags: supports -c / --c-to-f (convert Celsius to Fahrenheit) and -f / --f-to-c (convert Fahrenheit to Celsius) together with -v / --value to provide a single value. Example: tempconvert --c-to-f --value 100",
